--- Statements other than SELECT are rejected
MySQL invalidate_query: OK
MySQL query: OK
MySQL query with INTO OUTFILE: OK
MySQL where: OK
MySQL update_field: OK
MySQL named collection invalidate_query: OK
MySQL query in the named collection: OK
PostgreSQL invalidate_query in the named collection: OK
ODBC where with a named collection: OK
PostgreSQL invalidate_query: OK
PostgreSQL query: OK
MySQL query is an expression: OK
ODBC invalidate_query: OK
--- What the database reads differently from ClickHouse is rejected
MySQL executable comment: OK
MySQL -- without a space: OK
MySQL comment in where: OK
Heredoc: OK
Typographic quotes: OK
PostgreSQL backslash: OK
ODBC square brackets: OK
--- Every way to create a dictionary from a definition is checked
ON CLUSTER: OK
ON CLUSTER, old DDL entry format: OK
CREATE OR REPLACE: OK
--- The source is evaluated once, so the stored query is the checked one
1	0
--- SELECT is accepted
MySQL: OK
MySQL with expressions: OK
PostgreSQL: OK
MySQL query of the definition replaces the query of the named collection: OK
--- A query of the named collection is checked at each load and at RESTORE, because the collection can change
Before the change, the load fails only to connect: OK
After the change, the load is rejected: OK
RESTORE is rejected, and the dictionary is not restored: OK
--- A named collection requires the privilege NAMED COLLECTION
Without the grant: denied, not created
1
0
Without the grant, ON CLUSTER: denied, not created
1
0
Without the grant, the name is an expression: denied, not created
1
0
Without the grant, the queries of the collection are not read: denied for the collection
1
0
With the grant: created
0
1
With the grant, the name is an expression: created
0
1
--- The collection name is evaluated once, so the stored collection is the authorized one
1	0
--- An ODBC source requires the privilege READ ON ODBC
Without the grant: denied, not created
1
0
With the grant: created
0
1
